  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nAfter this current short wave trough departs the area this \nafternoon, dry weather will dominate through the holiday weekend. A \ndeep trough will move through the Midwest from Wednesday into \nThursday sending a reinforcing surface ridge into the area for \nThanksgiving. This will disrupt the warming trend that will occur \nfor the rest of the week. Saturday will be the warmest day of the \nweek with surface cyclogenesis in lee of the Rockies. Breezy to \nstrong downsloping westerly winds will contribute to the increased \nwarming on Saturday. This will be followed by another cold front on \nSunday knocking temperatures back down below seasonal averages. At \nthe moment, Monday is setting up to revert back to normal winter \ntime conditions of strong downsloping westerly winds.",
